    cml:premiseText "(2) In addition to any other matters, in determining whether the bail authority is satisfied that circumstances exist to grant bail to a person..." ;
    cml:conclusionText "The bail authority must not grant bail to the person." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .

concept:c2020a00070-sch-7-sec-4-ss-2 cml:asserts concept:c2020a00070-sch-7-sec-4-ss-2-logic-deontic-2 .
concept:c2020a00070-sch-7-sec-4-ss-2-logic-deontic-2 a cml:LogicApplication ;
    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    cml:operator "Prohibit" ;
    cml:logicSummary "Grants prohibition on granting bail to individuals who would not comply with conditions" ;
    cml:premiseText "(f) if the person has pleaded guilty to the charge in respect of the offence or been convicted of the offence—whether the bail authority considers that the person would not be likely to undertake a rehabilitation program, or not be likely to comply with any bail conditions relating to rehabilitation or treatment, while released on bail." ;
    cml:conclusionText "The bail authority must not grant bail to the person if they would not comply with conditions." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sch-7-sec-4-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "4(2) After section 15AA" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) In addition to any other matters, in determining whether the bail authority is satisfied that circumstances exist to grant bail to a person, the bail authority must take into account such of the following matters as are relevant and known to the bail authority:  (a) whether the bail authority considers that the person would be likely to fail to appear at any proceedings for the offence if the person were granted bail;  (b) whether the bail authority considers that the person would be likely to commit a further offence if the person were granted bail;  (c) whether the bail authority considers that the person would be likely to put at risk the safety of the community or cause a person to suffer any harm if the person were granted bail;  (d) whether the bail authority considers that the person would be likely to conceal, fabricate or destroy evidence or intimidate a witness if the person were granted bail;  Presumption against bail  Schedule 7 Commonwealth child sex offenders  Part 2  No. 70, 2020 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and Community Protection Measures) Act 2020  (e) whether the person was aged 18 years or over when the offence was committed;  (f) if the person has pleaded guilty to the charge in respect of the offence or been convicted of the offence—whether the bail authority considers that the person would not be likely to undertake a rehabilitation program, or not be likely to comply with any bail conditions relating to rehabilitation or treatment, while released on bail." ;
    cof:pageNumber "40"^^xsd:integer .

concept:c2020a00070-sch-7-sec-4-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "4(3) After section 15AA"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-7-sec-4-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) If the bail authority is a court and it grants bail, the court must:  (a) state its reasons; and  (b) cause those reasons to be entered in the court’s records." ;
    skos:definition "(3) If the bail authority is a court and it grants bail, the court must:  (a) state its reasons; and  (b) cause those reasons to be entered in the court’s records."@en ;
