    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) Despite any law of the Commonwealth, the Director of Public Prosecutions or the person may appeal against a decision of a bail authority:  (a) to grant bail to the person despite subsection (1) on the basis that the bail authority is satisfied that circumstances exist to grant bail; or  (b) to refuse to grant bail to the person on the basis that the bail authority is not satisfied that circumstances exist to grant bail." ;
