doc:sch-13-sec-19aq-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "19AQ(3) Parole order or licence revoked following further offence" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) A revocation time determined under subsection (1) or (2) must be one of the following times:  (a) the time at which the court determines the new offence was committed;  (b) the time at which the court determines the new offence was most likely to have been committed;  (c) the time at which the court determines the new offence was most likely to have first begun to have been committed. Time person liable to serve" ;
    cof:pageNumber "53"^^xsd:integer .

concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-19aq-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "19AQ(4) Parole order or licence revoked following further offence"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-13-sec-19aq-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) If the parole order or licence relating to a person is taken to have been revoked under subsection (1) or (2), the person becomes liable to serve:  Schedule 13  Revocation of parole order or licence  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and Community Protection Measures) Act 2020 No. 70, 2020  (a) that part of the sentence or of each sentence for a federal offence that the person had not served at the time of his or her release under that order or licence; or  (b) if the court considers it appropriate taking into account the good behaviour of the person during the period (the clean street period) starting at the time the person was released under that order or licence and ending at the revocation time—the sentence or aggregate sentence that would be imposed under paragraph (a) reduced by the period that is the same as the clean street period. Suspended sentences" ;
    skos:definition "(4) If the parole order or licence relating to a person is taken to have been revoked under subsection (1) or (2), the person becomes liable to serve:  Schedule 13  Revocation of parole order or licence  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and Community Protection Measures) Act 2020 No. 70, 2020  (a) that part of the sentence or of each sentence for a federal offence that the person had not served at the time of his or her release under that order or licence; or  (b) if the court considers it appropriate taking into account the good behaviour of the person during the period (the clean street period) starting at the time the person was released under that order or licence and ending at the revocation time—the sentence or aggregate sentence that would be imposed under paragraph (a) reduced by the period that is the same as the clean street period. Suspended sentences"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6a4c29cea6bf72027bd0cd7ee1989350cd730bb2da91b3d499b99dd868b8c4cc" ;
    values:partOf concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-19aq ;
    cof:pageNumber "53"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Parole order or licence revoked following further offence" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
