concept:c2020a00070-sch-13-sec-7 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "7 Subsections 19AR(1) and (2)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-13-sec-7 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the subsections, substitute: New federal offence etc.  (1) Subject to subsection (4), if:  (a) a person who is serving or is to serve a federal sentence or federal sentences is released on parole or licence under this Act; and  (b) the person is later sentenced (the new sentence or sentences) to a term of imprisonment in respect of a federal offence or federal offences committed during the parole period or licence period; and  (c) under section 19AQ:  (i) the parole order or licence is to be taken to have been revoked; and  Revocation of parole order or licence  Schedule 13  No. 70, 2020 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and Community Protection Measures) Act 2020  (ii) the person becomes liable to serve a part of a sentence or sentences (the outstanding sentence or sentences); the court imposing the new sentence or sentences:  (d) must not make a recognizance release order; and  (e) must fix a single new non-parole period in respect of the new sentence or sentences and the outstanding sentence or sentences having regard to the total period of imprisonment that the person is liable to serve." ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the subsections, substitute: New federal offence etc.  (1) Subject to subsection (4), if:  (a) a person who is serving or is to serve a federal sentence or federal sentences is released on parole or licence under this Act; and  (b) the person is later sentenced (the new sentence or sentences) to a term of imprisonment in respect of a federal offence or federal offences committed during the parole period or licence period; and  (c) under section 19AQ:  (i) the parole order or licence is to be taken to have been revoked; and  Revocation of parole order or licence  Schedule 13  No. 70, 2020 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Sexual Crimes Against Children and Community Protection Measures) Act 2020  (ii) the person becomes liable to serve a part of a sentence or sentences (the outstanding sentence or sentences); the court imposing the new sentence or sentences:  (d) must not make a recognizance release order; and  (e) must fix a single new non-parole period in respect of the new sentence or sentences and the outstanding sentence or sentences having regard to the total period of imprisonment that the person is liable to serve."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8a902efeba4290f256b95ce2cd9b467aa2b26cc23397877abf74c3580458d70a" ;
